c67b741e8f6bd8d64adbdb15e059d47fde004c77:corpus/lessons/round-50.md:32:- **Registry ids.** The planned rows were S243-S249 (S243-S245 and S249 were not registered, see `## Honest stop`; S246-S248 landed), not S150-S156: S150-S242 are cited in earlier lessons as refused staged rows that were never registered (`git grep -c S150 7c678ae6 -- corpus` finds only lessons; `w1/C1SrcFreetz.md` F6, `w1/C1SrcUnblob.md`), so reusing S150 would have made 239 historical citations point at a different source. The registry therefore skips S150-S242; this is stated, not repaired.
c67b741e8f6bd8d64adbdb15e059d47fde004c77:corpus/lessons/round-50.md:34:- **Assimilation (theme: AVM LE, `merge/kaidoku/`, read-only; no campaign tool run).** Guard receipts `.ufo/waves/round-50/assimilation/`: the staged ids S106-S237 and the registry ids S001-S149 overlap in **44** ids (S106-S149), **0 of 44** naming the same source (`collisions`); the guard is proven on a scratch registry whose only row is indented (`  | S106 |`): the 0-3-space pattern reports `S106`, the column-zero-only pattern reports nothing (`assimilation/guard-proof/`); the quarantine slice has 5 data rows (S113, S117, S136, S147, S150), each carrying an S-id, none of them cited by the two AVM-LE entries. Nothing was appended as-is; renumbering is by document, never arithmetic. **Admit (not registered):** the Freetz patch source (staged S206; planned as S243), re-opened with this lane's date and quote; no landed entry cites it. **Refuse (knowledge entries, reasons and flips recorded):** `avm-le-image-genuine-marker` — its evidence is lane-internal campaign TSVs (`lanes/kaidoku/round13/...`) that do not exist in this lane, the word "genuine" names a lane-built 4,096-byte image rather than vendor firmware (the C1 entry now holds real members), its recipe note is wrong (the plain `AVM_LE` build already sets the marker; patch 613 only makes it optional), and "upstream" is Freetz; flip: a round that lands the nine corrections in `w1/AssimGate.md` with the imported fixture and its own pins. `avm-le-variant-reachability` — its headline ("not reachable") is falsified (a stale-binary artefact); flip: a corrections-only rewrite keeping the three surviving facts. The `considerthese/` directory does not exist in this lane.
